<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for Altrune.app, signed with the hardened runtime (tools/firmar.sh).

  Altrune's own process needs none of the exceptions that weaken the hardened runtime: it has no
  JIT and no unsigned executable memory (no allow-jit, no allow-unsigned-executable-memory),
  it reads no DYLD environment variables (no allow-dyld-environment-variables) and it loads only
  system libraries and frameworks (no disable-library-validation). Wine and the engines Altrune
  downloads run as separate processes (on the test Mac their executables are not signed at all);
  the hardened runtime is a flag of each process, and whether they start under a Developer ID
  signed Altrune has not been tried.

  The one key below is for Apple events. Altrune starts /usr/bin/osascript to tell Terminal to
  open a console window for a bottle (src/backend/tools.rs, terminal_command_for). The events
  are sent by osascript, but Altrune is the process responsible for them, so under the hardened
  runtime Altrune carries the automation entitlement and Info.plist carries the usage text that
  macOS shows when it asks for permission (NSAppleEventsUsageDescription). Not yet tried on a
  signed and notarised build: see docs/firma-y-notarizacion.md.

  Adding a key here is a decision for review: tests/firma.rs lists the exact set.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
